            <ArticleTitle>[The adequacy and safety of low epidural anesthesia in urological operations on patients with concomitant ischemic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An electrocardiographic evaluation of the functional state of the myocardium in patients operated upon for urological diseases under conditions of low epidural anesthesia has shown that in the absence of a cardiovascular pathology the method of anesthesia fails to exert a substantial influence on the circulation homeokinesis and functional state of the myocardium. The following use of the low epidural anesthesia in 105 patients with a coexistent ischemic heart disease during urological operative interventions results in two times less amount of cardiovascular complications, lethality and duration of the postoperative period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
